## User Roles

### CUSTOMER
- Can register, log in, browse facilities, and book slots
- Views slot availability in real-time
- Completes payment via Razorpay checkout
- Receives booking confirmation email
- Can cancel a confirmed booking up to 2 hours before the slot starts
- Can join/leave the waitlist for fully-booked slots
- Views personal booking history (only confirmed and paid-then-cancelled bookings are shown)

### OWNER
- Can register, log in, and create/manage their own facilities
- Adds courts under each facility with sport type and pricing
- Generates time slots in bulk with configurable parameters
- Cannot book slots (booking is restricted to CUSTOMER role)
- Views the analytics dashboard: revenue, occupancy, upcoming bookings, recent activity
- Receives an email with customer name and contact when a booking is confirmed
- Can delete courts (confirmation required) and facilities (password verification required)

---

## Booking Flow

```
1. DISCOVER
   Customer opens Home page → browser requests geolocation
   → Backend queries facilities within radius using Haversine formula
   → Results displayed on Leaflet map + card grid sorted by distance

2. SELECT
   Customer opens a facility → selects a court → selects a date
   → Frontend requests slots for that court/date
   → Past slots (IST-aware) shown as disabled
   → Available slots shown in colour-coded grid

3. INITIATE
   Customer clicks an available slot
   → POST /api/bookings/initiate
   → Backend runs atomic updateMany: slot AVAILABLE → LOCKED (only one transaction succeeds)
   → Razorpay order created → order_id returned to frontend

4. PAYMENT
   Frontend opens Razorpay checkout modal with order_id
   → Customer enters card/UPI details
   → On success: Razorpay returns { payment_id, order_id, signature }

5. CONFIRM
   Frontend calls POST /api/bookings/confirm with Razorpay response
   → Backend verifies HMAC-SHA256 signature against key_secret
   → On valid: booking → CONFIRMED, slot → BOOKED, payment → PAID
   → Confirmation email sent to customer
   → Notification email sent to owner
   → Socket.io emits slot_updated to all clients viewing that facility

6. REAL-TIME
   All other customers viewing the same facility see the slot
   change colour (green → grey) instantly via Socket.io — no page refresh

7. ABANDON
   If customer closes Razorpay or navigates back without paying:
   → BookingConfirm cleanup fires POST /api/bookings/:id/cancel
   → PENDING booking record deleted entirely (not marked CANCELLED)
   → Slot returns to AVAILABLE
   → Slot update emitted via Socket.io
```

