## Database Design

### Entities and Relationships

```
USERS (1) ─────────────────────────────── (many) FACILITIES
  │ (customer)                                        │
  │ (many)                                        (many) COURTS
  │                                                    │
  └──────────── (many) BOOKINGS ◄──── (1) SLOTS ─────┘
                          │              │
                      (1) PAYMENT    (many) WAITLIST ──► (many) USERS
```

### Models

| Model | Key Fields | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| **User** | id, name, email, passwordHash, role, refreshToken | Role: OWNER or CUSTOMER |
| **Facility** | id, ownerId, name, address, city, latitude, longitude, imageUrl, imageUrls[] | Multi-image support |
| **Court** | id, facilityId, name, sportType, basePrice | Belongs to one Facility |
| **Slot** | id, courtId, startTime, endTime, price, status | Status: AVAILABLE / LOCKED / BOOKED / CANCELLED |
| **Booking** | id, slotId (@unique), userId, status, totalAmount | @unique on slotId prevents double-booking at DB level |
| **Payment** | id, bookingId (@unique), razorpayOrderId, razorpayPaymentId, amount, status | Status: CREATED / PAID / FAILED / REFUNDED |
| **Waitlist** | id, slotId, userId, position | @unique([slotId, userId]) — one entry per user per slot |

### Key Constraints
- `Booking.slotId` has `@unique` — one booking per slot enforced at the database level
- `Facility → Court → Slot` uses `onDelete: Cascade` — deleting a facility removes all child records
- `Waitlist` has `@unique([slotId, userId])` — prevents duplicate waitlist entries

