## API Overview

### Authentication — `/api/auth`
| Method | Endpoint | Auth | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| POST | `/register` | Public | Create account (OWNER or CUSTOMER) |
| POST | `/login` | Public | Login, returns access + refresh tokens |
| POST | `/refresh` | Public | Rotate tokens using refresh token |
| POST | `/logout` | Bearer | Clear refresh token |
| GET | `/me` | Bearer | Get current user profile |
| POST | `/verify-password` | Bearer | Verify password before destructive actions |

### Facilities — `/api/facilities`
| Method | Endpoint | Auth | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| GET | `/nearby?lat=&lng=&radius=` | Public | Find facilities by coordinates (Haversine) |
| GET | `/my` | OWNER | List owner's own facilities |
| GET | `/:id` | Public | Get facility details with courts |
| POST | `/` | OWNER | Create facility (multipart/form-data, 1–4 images) |
| PUT | `/:id` | OWNER | Update facility |
| DELETE | `/:id` | OWNER | Delete facility and all child data |
| GET | `/:facilityId/analytics` | OWNER | Revenue, occupancy, and booking stats |
| GET | `/:facilityId/courts` | Public | List courts for a facility |
| POST | `/:facilityId/courts` | OWNER | Add a court to a facility |
| DELETE | `/:facilityId/courts/:courtId` | OWNER | Delete a court |

### Courts — `/api/courts`
| Method | Endpoint | Auth | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| PUT | `/:courtId` | OWNER | Update court details |
| POST | `/:courtId/slots/generate` | OWNER | Generate slots for a date range |
| GET | `/:courtId/slots?date=` | Public | Get slots for a court on a given date |

### Bookings — `/api/bookings`
| Method | Endpoint | Auth | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| POST | `/initiate` | CUSTOMER | Lock slot + create Razorpay order |
| POST | `/confirm` | CUSTOMER | Verify HMAC signature + confirm booking |
| GET | `/my` | CUSTOMER | Customer's booking history |
| GET | `/:id` | Bearer | Single booking detail |
| POST | `/:id/cancel` | Bearer | Cancel booking + release slot |
| GET | `/facility/:facilityId` | OWNER | All bookings for a facility |

### Waitlist — `/api/waitlist`
| Method | Endpoint | Auth | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| POST | `/join` | CUSTOMER | Join waitlist for a booked slot |
| DELETE | `/leave/:slotId` | CUSTOMER | Leave waitlist |

### Webhooks — `/api/webhooks`
| Method | Endpoint | Auth | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| POST | `/razorpay` | Razorpay signature | Handle payment.captured and payment.failed events |

---

## Authentication & Security

### Token Strategy
- **Access token** — short-lived JWT (15 minutes in production), signed with `ACCESS_TOKEN_SECRET`
- **Refresh token** — long-lived JWT (7 days), signed with `REFRESH_TOKEN_SECRET`
- Refresh tokens are **SHA-256 hashed** before storage in the database — raw tokens are never persisted
- Every `/refresh` call issues a completely new token pair (**token rotation**) — stolen tokens expire after one use
- On logout, the stored refresh token is set to `null`

### Password Security
- Passwords hashed with **bcryptjs** at 12 salt rounds
- Login errors return the same generic message whether the email doesn't exist or the password is wrong (prevents user enumeration)
- Destructive actions (facility deletion) require the user to re-enter their password via a dedicated `/verify-password` endpoint, not the login endpoint, so tokens are never regenerated mid-session

### Concurrent Booking Protection
- Slot locking uses `prisma.slot.updateMany({ where: { id, status: 'AVAILABLE' }, data: { status: 'LOCKED' } })` inside a `$transaction`
- Because `updateMany` is atomic, only one of N simultaneous requests can change the status — all others get `count: 0` and are rejected
- Verified with a 5-parallel-request stress test (`tests/concurrent-booking.test.js`)

### Payment Verification
- After Razorpay payment, the backend recreates the HMAC-SHA256 signature from `orderId|paymentId` using the Razorpay key secret
- Booking is only confirmed if the computed signature matches the one sent by Razorpay — fake payments are rejected

### Role Authorisation
- `verifyToken` middleware — validates JWT on every protected route
- `checkRole('OWNER' | 'CUSTOMER')` middleware — checks the role claim in the JWT payload
- Ownership checks are enforced in controllers (e.g. owners can only modify their own facilities)

