## Environment Variables

### Server (`server/.env`)
```env
# PostgreSQL (Neon or any PostgreSQL provider)
DATABASE_URL=

# JWT
ACCESS_TOKEN_SECRET=
ACCESS_TOKEN_EXPIRY=15m
REFRESH_TOKEN_SECRET=
REFRESH_TOKEN_EXPIRY=7d

# Razorpay
RAZORPAY_KEY_ID=
RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET=
RAZORPAY_WEBHOOK_SECRET=

# Cloudinary
CLOUDINARY_CLOUD_NAME=
CLOUDINARY_API_KEY=
CLOUDINARY_API_SECRET=

# Email (Gmail SMTP — use an App Password, not your account password)
EMAIL_USER=
EMAIL_PASS=
EMAIL_FROM=

# App
PORT=5000
NODE_ENV=development
FRONTEND_URL=http://localhost:5173
```

### Client (`client/.env`)
```env
VITE_API_URL=http://localhost:5000/api
```

---

## Local Setup

### Prerequisites
- Node.js 18+
- A PostgreSQL database (local or cloud — [Neon](https://neon.tech) free tier works)
- A [Cloudinary](https://cloudinary.com) account (free tier)
- A [Razorpay](https://razorpay.com) test account
- A Gmail account with an [App Password](https://support.google.com/accounts/answer/185833) generated

### 1. Clone the repository

```bash
git clone https://github.com/your-username/turfly.git
cd turfly
```

### 2. Backend setup

```bash
cd server
npm install
cp .env.example .env   # Fill in all required values
```

### 3. Frontend setup

```bash
cd ../client
npm install
cp .env.example .env   # Set VITE_API_URL
```

### 4. Run both servers

```bash
# Terminal 1 — Backend
cd server
npm run dev

# Terminal 2 — Frontend
cd client
npm run dev
```

Frontend: `http://localhost:5173`
Backend: `http://localhost:5000`

---

## Database Setup

### Run migrations

```bash
cd server
npx prisma migrate dev --name init
```

### Generate Prisma client (after schema changes)

```bash
npx prisma generate
```

### Seed demo data

Populates 10 facilities across Mumbai, Delhi, Bangalore, and Pune with 2 courts each, plus a demo owner and customer account.

```bash
node prisma/seed.js
```

**Demo credentials after seeding:**
| Role | Email | Password |
|---|---|---|
| Owner | `owner@turfly.com` | `Demo@1234` |
| Customer | `customer@turfly.com` | `Demo@1234` |

### Inspect database (Prisma Studio)

```bash
npx prisma studio
```

### Run concurrent booking stress test

```bash
# Update SLOT_ID and CUSTOMER_TOKEN in the file first
node tests/concurrent-booking.test.js
```

Expected output:
```
✅ user-1: Booking initiated
❌ user-2: This slot has just been booked by someone else.
❌ user-3: This slot has just been booked by someone else.
❌ user-4: This slot has just been booked by someone else.
❌ user-5: This slot has just been booked by someone else.
```

